                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Played this immediately after finishing BL2 and noticed the gulf in quality within a couple moments. \r\n\r\nThis game is annoying af and holds your hand through every single moment of play, particularly in the early missions where the prompts are almost constant when you just want to take a few moments to explore and see what the world has to offer. You end up rushing from waypoint to waypoint just to shut the stupid thing up.\r\n\r\nOn top of this the characterisatiuons are suuuuuuper annoying - as an aussie the heavy australian flavour used here is especially grating, unnatural (even for the slang) and is absolutely generated to sound fun but unoffensive to an interantional audience. \r\n\r\nCertain characters make it painfully clear of their personal stories from the off without the player needing to do anything to uncover the layers each person they meet may have to them.\r\n\r\nIn short, the magic of BL2 is lost here through clunky exposition, unfunny dialogue and an overly obnoxious aussie attitude that is neither entertaining or understandable to anyone except those from Down Under.\r\n\r\nAdd it to your collection if you want the set, but dont look at this one as the definitive BL experience.",
